; =====================================================================
; cose-hash.derived.cddl
;
; DERIVED -- NOT verbatim.  This file is this library's, not RFC 9054's.
; Do not cite it as the standard's grammar; cite
; cose-hash-structures.cddl, which holds the source's own bytes with the
; erratum intact.
;
; It is RFC 9054 section 2.1's two fragments with exactly three mechanical
; changes and no others:
;
;   1. erratum 7335 applied - every `#` comment marker becomes `;`;
;   2. COSE_Hash_V given the `{ }` the document never supplies, as a
;      separate rule, so it can be the root of a model;
;   3. the left margin removed.
;
; No member key, type, occurrence indicator or comment TEXT was added,
; removed, reordered or retyped.  Checked by round-trip: re-indenting
; and re-substituting `#` for `;` reproduces the verbatim regions byte
; for byte, and the generator aborts if it does not.
;
; WHY (2) IS NEEDED, AND IT IS NOT A STYLE POINT.  `COSE_Hash_V = ( ... )`
; is a parenthesised GROUP, not a type: its entries carry member keys
; (`1 :`, `2 :`), and RFC 8610's grammar can only parse the rule as a
; group rule - forced as a type rule it fails after 14 characters
; (cddl-parse.derived.txt).  RFC 8610 section 2.2.4 then says "there is no way
; to use a group as a root -- it must be a type" (quoted in this
; library's records/ietf/rfc-8610/distilled/schema/
; grammar-gaps.derived.txt, item G-04).  So the fragment as printed, even
; with the erratum applied, cannot be instantiated: SOMETHING must wrap
; it, and RFC 9054 never says what.  A map is the only wrapper the
; member keys permit - RFC 8610 Appendix C, via G-03: "If the memberkey
; is not given, the entry can only be used for matching arrays, not for
; maps", and these keys ARE given.
;
; CONTRAST COSE_Hash_Find, which parses AS PRINTED and as a TYPE rule,
; because `[ ... ]` is `type2`.  Two structures, one document, one
; usable.
;
; Requirement ids: rfc-9054#R-0043 (the printed structure), rfc-9054#R-0042 (its
; status as an example), rfc-9054#R-0045 (the second structure), rfc-9054#R-0037 to
; rfc-9054#R-0040 (the four fields as prose), rfc-9054#R-0041 (the length rule).
; =====================================================================

; --- (1) + (3): erratum 7335 applied, margin removed.  STILL A GROUP.
COSE_Hash_V = (
    1 : int / tstr, ; Algorithm identifier
    2 : bstr, ; Hash value
    ? 3 : tstr, ; Location of object that was hashed
    ? 4 : any   ; object containing other details and things
    )

; --- (2): the wrapper the document never supplies.  OURS.
COSE_Hash_V_map = { COSE_Hash_V }

; --- RFC 9054's second fragment, margin removed.  Already a type.
COSE_Hash_Find = [
    hashAlg : int / tstr,
    hashValue : bstr
]

; =====================================================================
; WHAT THIS LIBRARY WOULD ACTUALLY WRITE, and why it is not either of
; the above.  Nothing below is RFC 9054's.
; =====================================================================
;
; RFC 9054 section 1 states that COSE "does not define a structure syntax that
; is used to encode a digested object structure along the lines of the
; DigestedData ASN.1 structure in [CMS]" (rfc-9054#R-0002) and that
; "This omission was intentional" (rfc-9054#R-0003).  So R-O-03's
; algorithm half is citable - the eight identifiers below - and its
; CARRIER half has nothing to cite.  The structure is ours to invent,
; and these two fragments are the closest prior art in COSE.
;
; The one constraint section 2.1 does supply is a canonicalization rule in
; disguise (rfc-9054#R-0041): additional data must "either be a fixed known
; size, or the lengths of the pieces being hashed be included so that
; the resulting byte string has a unique interpretation as the
; additional data.  (Encoding as a CBOR array accomplishes this
; requirement.)"  That is `canonical-encoding` condition (1) -
; injectivity - argued in a parenthetical, with no keyword.

mofn-hash = [
    alg: mofn-hash-alg,        ; section 2.1 field 1, and it is INSIDE the
                               ; digested structure, not beside it
    value: bstr,               ; section 2.1 field 2
    ? located-at: tstr,        ; section 2.1 field 3
    ? aad: [* bstr]            ; section 2.1 field 4, as a CBOR array -
                               ; which is section 2.1's own answer to the
                               ; unique-interpretation problem
]

; The eight identifiers RFC 9054 registers, as a CDDL type.  THIS IS THE
; CITATION R-O-03 NEEDS.  -14 and -15 are excluded here and present in
; the registry; see ../../rfc-9360/distilled/schema/
; x5t-hashalg-policy.derived.yaml for the per-value reasoning.
mofn-hash-alg = -16 / -17 / -18 / -43 / -44 / -45
cose-hash-alg-all = -14 / -15 / -16 / -17 / -18 / -43 / -44 / -45
